import json,shutil,os,hashlib
b=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;s=b/'stage/56044dcd81ce';d=s/'astraupskill';images=d/'images';images.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
for name in ['desktop','narrow']:shutil.copy2(b/f'checks/workforce/browser/{name}.png',images/f'{name}.png')
(d/'VERIFICATION.md').write_text('''# Verification evidence and limits

The delivered worker directory was checked in an isolated project copy with Node 22.16.0, Prisma 5.22.0, PostgreSQL 18.1, Playwright 1.60.0 and Chromium 148. All 29 API integration tests passed. All eight browser scenarios passed without skips or retries. The API type check, API build, frontend type check, frontend production build and frontend lint passed. The fresh migration applied successfully, and the demo seed completed twice against the owned test database.

The API evidence includes salted password verification, sign-in, protected requests, account/tenant suspension checks, unsupported roles, create/read/update/delete, a resolvable create Location, strict payload/query bounds, per-tenant normalized email uniqueness, real competing creates and updates, foreign item IDs, a direct database attempt to assign a foreign company, inactive company rejection, lifecycle guards, stale deletion and related-history protection. A temporary database trigger rejected audit insertion after a profile update; querying afterward confirmed that the update rolled back. Generic error responses carried request references instead of SQL details.

Browser evidence covers CRUD across sign-out/sign-in, confirmed deletion with retained audit history, duplicate rejection preserving the draft, two-tab conflicts, explicit current-record reload, lifecycle controls, a read-only terminated profile, tenant switching, synthetic server failure, literal markup-like names, search empty state and responsive layouts. The [desktop capture](images/desktop.png) and [narrow capture](images/narrow.png) were visually reviewed. On narrow screens the directory table intentionally scrolls horizontally inside its panel; the page itself stays within the viewport. These captures are not a comprehensive accessibility certification.

Verification used fresh helper-owned clusters and synthetic accounts. Each cluster was stopped before its temporary directory was removed. Windows PostgreSQL startup uses file-backed command output so an inherited daemon pipe does not keep the runner waiting. Browser test configuration also requires the owned test-database marker, loopback host and test database name. The final browser phase was rerun after correcting workspace Vite resolution; the unchanged API suite's 29 passing results were retained as separate evidence. Logs and machine-readable results are recorded in the parent workspace's implementation checks and delivery manifest.

No existing personal database was migrated, seeded or queried for test fixtures. The initial migration targets an empty database; a populated installation needs a reviewed baselining/data-migration plan. The supplied Docker configuration was not run because a Docker daemon was unavailable. Authentication remains a local learning implementation without MFA, refresh sessions, distributed throttling or a global administrator console. The UI keeps its token in memory and reload signs out. There is no create-idempotency receipt, external notification outbox or crash/power-loss test. Company maintenance, worker self-service and the other EOR domains remain exercises or schema-only material. Request-time account checks do not cancel an already executing transaction when an account changes later.
''',encoding='utf-8')
